Z||000000||My7Fieros||09-08-2001||10:44 PM||||Awhile back I worked part time at a leather goods/ arts and crafts type store (a friend owned) and bought some leather. Well I found a piece of a silvery metallic leather (real leather, not vynle)and a piece of 'standard' grey leather I had bought back then and was wondering what I could do with it. Well tonight my roommate popped out the old sewing machine and made a shift boot. He's gonna put this one in his GT.. Check it......<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-015s_4.jpg">   <BR>I made this one out of the piece of 'regular' grey leather and put it in my SE...<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-017s_5.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-018s_4.jpg">  <BR>Its not perfect, but all in all its not too bad for an hours worth of work I dont think!<BR> <P><BR>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I><P><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||10
