Z||000006||sqoach||09-10-2001||12:29 AM||||Looks good! I made one for my shortened shifter. All by hand, too! What a b!tch that was! Then it turned out to be a little bit short for the shifter. Now I need to shorten up my shifter even more. Oh well, still looks neat  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Hey Tonker, you interested in a short shifter? E-mail me.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">        <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC (FOR SALE)</FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000007||My7Fieros||09-10-2001||01:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tonker:<BR><B>Are you aware that you have a filing cabinet in your Fiero?<P>Very nice, though!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Is that a short shifter, BTW? Where did you pick it up and how difficult to install?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Lol, yes Im aware of the 'filing cabinet'..its my tote box of paper work I carry in the squad car (offense reports, tickets, ect.).<BR>Also that is a shortened shifter, I made it myself. I simply cut a part of the original shifter, rethreaded it, and cut a small piece off the bottom of the knob.<P><P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
